edge_count: 2
complexity: time=O(n) | space=O(1)
complexity_note: n is the number of nodes.
why_time: One walk with slow and fast.
why_space: Only three pointers are kept.
hint: The starter returns None when there's only one node.
hint: While fast and fast.next aren't None: `prev = slow`, then move slow one node and fast two.
hint: `prev.next = slow.next`, then return head.
right: prev trails slow by one node, so when slow stops on the middle, the node before it is ready to relink, all in one walk.
wrong: Handle one node first. Otherwise walk slow and fast with prev one node behind slow, then link prev past slow and return the head.

