Frame the windows with two pointers k nodes apart. First move lead k nodes on, adding up the first window. Then, while lead isn't None, the current window starts at lag: write its total into lag, and slide the window on by one. Writing into lag overwrites a value the total still has to take off, so save it first: `old = lag.val`, then `lag.val = total` and `total += lead.val - old`. When lead runs out, lag is the start of the last window: write its total there and end the list after it.

